          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">What Warranties Actually Cover</h3>

          <p>
            A ten-year limited warranty usually covers manufacturing defects and visible sagging or body impressions beyond a stated depth. It typically excludes normal softening, stains, damage from an unsupportive base, and resale. Purple, for example, states that its warranty applies to the original purchaser for personal use.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">How to Use Them</h3>

          <p>
            Buy from the brand's storefront or from Amazon itself, keep the receipt, put a <a href="/best-mattress-protector/">mattress protector</a> on from night one, and use the base the brand specifies. Those four steps keep both the trial and the warranty intact. For timing a purchase, see our <a href="/mattress-prices-and-deals/">mattress prices and deals</a> guide.
          </p>
