          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            11. Frequently Asked Questions
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the best mattress brand?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                For most buyers on Amazon, Nectar is the best mattress brand overall because it states a 365-night trial and a Forever Warranty, and its medium-firm beds suit most sleepers. Casper is the best for zoned support, Purple for hot sleepers, Sealy for edge support, and Zinus for the lowest price. Choose the model by firmness first.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What are the top 5 mattress brands?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Among brands sold on Amazon, five strong choices are Nectar, Casper, Purple, Tuft & Needle and Sealy. Nectar leads on trial length, Casper on zoned support, Purple on cooling, Tuft & Needle on simple mid-priced hybrids and Sealy on edge support. Serta and Zinus are close behind for value. The best of them for you depends on the model.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Are online mattress brands as good as store brands?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Often, yes. Online brands built the long sleep trial into their business, and many sell hybrids with the same kinds of foam and coils as store beds. Legacy brands like Sealy and Serta now sell boxed lines online too. The main difference is that you cannot try a boxed mattress first, so the trial and return terms matter more.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Which mattress brand has the best warranty?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Of the brands here, Nectar states the strongest warranty, its Forever Warranty, along with a 365-night trial. Casper, Purple, Tuft & Needle, Serta and Sealy list ten-year limited warranties. Read what each covers: most cover defects and sagging beyond a stated depth, and exclude normal softening, stains and damage from an unsupportive base.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is Zinus a good mattress brand?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Zinus is a good budget brand. Its Green Tea memory foam mattresses are among the most popular on Amazon, list CertiPUR-US certified foam and cost far less than premium brands. The trade-off is lower-density foam that tends to soften sooner, and owners commonly report a new-foam smell at first. It suits guest rooms, kids and first apartments best.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Who owns Tuft & Needle?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Amazon listings for Tuft & Needle mattresses name Serta Simmons Bedding as the manufacturer on some models and Fosbrooke, Inc. doing business as Tuft & Needle on others. In practice the brand still sells its own range with its stated 100-night trial and 10-year limited warranty. Keep your receipt and listing in case you need to make a warranty claim.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Should I buy a mattress brand on Amazon or direct?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Either can work. Most brands here run official Amazon storefronts, and buying from the brand or Amazon itself usually keeps the brand's trial and warranty. Buying direct can make returns simpler, because only one company is involved. Compare the price, the return process and the seller before ordering, and avoid unauthorized third-party sellers.
              </p>
            </div>

          </div>
